WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.700
Nigeria has the highest rate of identical
twins.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.280
China has the lowest rate at only 1 in 300
births being twins.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.800
Polar bears most commonly give birth to twins.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.500
22% of twins are left handed, compared to
only 10% of non-twins.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.410
Researchers suspect that 1 in 8 people start
life as a twin but because of miscarriages

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:35.660
of one of the fetuses, only 1 in 70 people
are actually born twins.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.410
That's all very interesting but...

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.480
What Actually Causes Twins?

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.160
There are two types of "Multiple Pregnancy",
identical and fraternal.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.820
Identical or monozygotic twins occur when
one egg is fertilised by one sperm and the

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.610
fertilised egg splits into two or more embryos.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:58.590
Scientists believe identical twins happen
purely by chance and there are no contributing

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:02.780
factors, such as age, race or family genes.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:08.420
One quarter of all twins are "mirror twins",
caused by a late split of the fertilised egg.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.850
This is when the twins are direct reflections
of each other.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:15.979
One will always be left handed and the other
will always be right handed.

00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:20.420
If one has a birthmark on the left side of
their face the other will have the same birthmark

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.950
on the right side, and so on.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:27.729
But the reflection is more than skin deep,
one of the twins will have their internal

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:33.609
organs on the wrong side of their body, so
their heart will beat on the right side.

00:01:33.609 --> 00:01:38.999
On the other hand fraternal or dizygotic twins
runs in the family.

00:01:38.999 --> 00:01:43.959
Fraternal pregnancy happens when two or more
eggs are fertilised by different sperm.

00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:49.469
Women can inherit a certain gene which causes
them to hyper-ovulate, meaning she is more

00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:52.859
likely to release multiple eggs during ovulation.

00:01:52.859 --> 00:01:56.130
Therefore, increasing the chance of a multiple
pregnancy.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:00.840
So if anyone in your family has twins, or
you yourself are a twin, you're much more

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.909
likely to have twins yourself.

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:05.289
The Rate of Twins is Increasing Dramatically

00:02:05.289 --> 00:02:09.959
The birth rate of twins has increased by 76%
since 1980.

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:18.019
In 1980 one in every 53 babies was a twin,
however today, one in every 30 babies born

00:02:18.019 --> 00:02:19.019
is a twin.

00:02:19.019 --> 00:02:22.319
Which, when you think about it, is an awful
lot of twins.

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:24.400
But what caused such an upsurge?

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.920
One of the biggest factor is that the average
age of women having children has risen, and

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.860
the older the mother is, the more likely she
is to give birth to twins.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:37.599
Another contributing factor is a rapid increase
in the use of fertility treatments that promote

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:39.680
the release of multiple eggs during ovulation.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.239
But enough of that, let's get onto the really
bizarre stuff...

00:02:43.239 --> 00:02:45.000
There's a "Twin Town"

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.430
A small town in Brazil, Cândido Godói is
the twin capital of the world.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:56.030
Amongst the 80 families that live in the town,
there are 38 pairs of twins.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:00.030
Some believe there's something in the water
that's causing such such an astronomically

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.959
high number of twin births.

00:03:01.959 --> 00:03:06.250
But others think there's something much more
sinister going on.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:11.819
Researchers have suggested it may have been
caused by a Nazi physician called Josef Mengele,

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:14.480
who had the nickname "Angel of Death".

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:20.769
It has been said that during the 1960s, when
the explosion of twins in the town first occurred,

00:03:20.769 --> 00:03:26.150
Mengele was performing experiments on the
women of the town, involving strange new drugs

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:30.209
and even artificial insemination.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:32.159
Identical Twins, Aren't Identical

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:35.999
All identical twins have distinguishable qualities
from birth.

00:03:35.999 --> 00:03:41.880
After all identical twins do have different
DNA, their DNA is extremely similar but not

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.769
identical.

00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:48.430
Identical twins also have completely different
sets of fingerprints.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.569
Twins Have Their Own Language

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:56.040
"Idioglossia" is a language shared between
twins, that only they understand.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:02.090
About 40% of twins invent their own language,
it sounds complete gibberish to me and you

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.190
but it's a close bond shared between the siblings.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:11.120
This phenomenon can also occur between very
close siblings, but more commonly twins.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.590
Their shared language usually disappears by
the time they start school.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:17.670
How Different Can Twins Be?

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:18.670
Very.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:24.090
Twins can be different genders, but even more
astonishing, twins can be different ages.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:29.640
Recently there was a case where 5 year old
Reuben Blake got a brand new twin sister.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:33.960
Even though they have 5 years between them,
they are still, technically twins.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:39.600
Their mother had difficulty getting pregnant
naturally so she turned to In vitro fertilisation

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.600
(IVF).

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:44.140
This is when the eggs are fertilised outside
of the body then re-implanted into the woman's

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.140
uterus.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:50.940
But Reuben's mother only had two of the embryos
from the process implanted into her uterus,

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.300
the other three were frozen.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:57.590
A few years later she had the remaining embryos
implanted and 9 months later she gave birth

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.940
to Reuben's twin sister.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.550
Believe it or not twins can have different
dads and be different races.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:09.570
It's rare, but about 2% of fraternal twins
have different dads.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:14.620
This happens when a woman releases two eggs
during ovulation and then gets impregnated

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.790
by two different men at the same time.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.060
Twins Bond in the Belly

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:24.720
We've all witnessed the unbreakable bond that
twins often have, but where does it come from?

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.380
Twins actually bond physically in the womb.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:33.320
Researchers at the University of Padova in
Italy noticed via 3D ultrasound that at 14

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:37.010
weeks old, fetuses reach out for each other
in the womb.

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:42.870
At 18 weeks old they were stroking each other
and maintained physical contact 30% of the

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:43.870
time.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:49.220
Strangely, in these tests the fetuses avoided
touching each other's eyes, as if they know

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.000
it's a delicate area.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:56.220
So now you know all about twins, but the story
I'm about to share with you will blow your

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.020
mind, introducing...

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.540
The Twin Jims

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:05.080
The prize for the most incredible twin story
has to go to Jim Lewis and Jim Springer.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:09.980
They were born in 1940 and adopted by separate
families in Ohio.

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:15.370
They grew up 45 miles from each other and
had no contact for 39 years.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:21.690
When they were reunited in 1979 they discovered
that they were both named James by their adoptive

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:27.680
parents, they both married twice, first to
women named Linda and secondly to women named

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.680
Betty.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:34.390
They both had children, Jim Springer had a
boy whom he named James Allan and Jim Lewis

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:39.990
named his son James Alan, with one L. They
both had dogs named Toy.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:44.470
They both drank the same beer, smoked the
same cigarettes and drove the same model of

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.290
car, Chevrolets.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:50.490
Their medical histories were identical and
they shared the same hobbies, including a

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:53.780
woodworking workshop in both their garages.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:57.790
They both had vacations on the exact same
beach in Florida.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:01.620
Simply incredible.

